      "message": "Can we explicitly name this as CcLibrarySharedLabel and CcLibraryStaticLabel to reduce the context switching?\n\nMoreover, I think it doesn\u0027t read well for `SyspropLibraryLabels` struct to have labels for cc libraries.\n\nIMO, one option to make this better is to have `Bp2buildSysprop` func to accept `syspropLibrary` object. This way, we can have\n\n```\npackage sysprop\n\nfunc (m *syspropLibrary) ConvertWithBp2build(ctx android.TopDownMutatorContext) {\n  cc.Bp2buildSysprop(ctx, m)\n}\n```\n\n```\npackage cc\n\nfunc Bp2buildSysprop(ctx android.Bp2buildMutatorContext, syspropLib syspropLibrary) {\n  syspropLibraryLabel :\u003d syspropLib.BaseModuleName()\n  ccLibrarySharedLabel :\u003d syspropLib.CcImplementationModuleName()\n  ccLibraryStaticLabel :\u003d cc.BazelLabelNameForStaticModule(ccLibrarySharedLabel)\n  // use the label vars directly here\n}\n```",
